<title>UK: RMC at six-month low on stock overhang.</title>
<headline>RMC at six-month low on stock overhang.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in RMC Group Plc fell on Wednesday to a six-month low as stock overhanging the market depressed the share price, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares dropped 23p to 970-1/2p by 1146 GMT, the lowest level since June 25.</p>
<p>&quot;There is stock overhanging the market and the sector is out of favour,&quot; said one market maker.</p>
<p>Shares in Redland Plc also fell, to be down 12p at 382-1/2p, the lowest since July 3.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
